Have you done the quest?  If not, that would be my
recommendation.  The Valk quest is a pushover if you know how to
avoid problems with drawbridges, and the quest artifact gives
half damage---its like having twice the hit points.  Not to
mention level teleport at will.  Also, since you have a robe,
check out the spell casting possibilities: with enough
intelligence and experience, you can cast some fairly useful
spells at 0% failure.  (Cure sickness is useful at certain very
precise times, and cone of cold is your role's special spell,
and can be useful as well.  Plus any number of others, for
occasional use.  On the other hand, I've also ascended without
ever casting a single spell.)

As a Valk, I'd have been two weaponing for a long time already.
Two weaponing Excalibur and the silver saber, for example, gives
all of the advantages of Excalibur, plus silver.  And you don't
mention speed: a Valk is naturally fast, and with speed boots,
doubly so.  Fast enough, in fact, that you can sometimes kill
the major demon before it even has time to teleport to the up
stairs.

I'd also see if I could get a ring of free action.  A ring of
free action and a wielded potion of paralysis, with the speed,
can pratically guarantee getting rid of the major demons in one
sitting.

For the rest: Grayswandir's about the only weapon better than
Excalibur, and even then... I sort of like Excalibur's intrinsic
searching.  (On the other hand, the RDG has given my current
Valk just about everything: 9 wishs before the castle, and 7 or
8 artifacts, including Grayswandir and Frosty.  So just for a
change, I've charged up Grayswandir and am twoweaponing it and a
silver saber.  Curious to see what twice silver damage can do.
That, along with the potions of paralysis, mean that Gehemmon
has been particularly easy so far.  None of the demons have ever
even touched me, and the only one left is Orcus.  Now if I only
hadn't prayed too soon *after* having finished off the wraiths
in the VoD; buying my protection back with XP29 is very
difficult.)

